<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Maghrawa emirate of Fez</h1><p class="st-meta">987 CE – 1070 CE (approx.) · capital Fez</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Zenata Berber emirate that ruled Fez and northern Morocco as allies of Córdoba, between the Idrisids and the Almoravids.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Maghrawa, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanata-berbers">Zenata Berber</a> tribe, became allies of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba</a> in its struggle with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>. Around 987 their chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziri-ibn-atiyya">Ziri ibn Atiyya</a> took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba's</a> governor, while another branch of the tribe had seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sijilmasa">Sijilmasa</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/midrarid-emirate">Midrarid emirate</a> in 976.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziri-ibn-atiyya">Ziri ibn Atiyya</a> founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oujda">Oujda</a> in 994. He rebelled against the Córdoban regent al-Mansur, was defeated in 998, and his son al-Mu'izz was restored as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> ruled through tribal alliances and the urban notables of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>, which grew as a centre of trade and learning. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba's</a> collapse in 1031 they ruled independently, though weakened by wars with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banu-ifran-emirate">Banu Ifran emirate</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 1060s the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> advanced from the south. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> around 1069 to 1070, ending Maghrawa rule in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-morocco">Morocco</a>. Fez went on to become a leading city of the Almoravid and later Moroccan states.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 987 CE – 1070 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.34%;width:1.65%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>987 CE – 1070 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fez</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ziri ibn Atiyya, al-Mu'izz ibn Ziri</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Maghrawa, Zenata emirate of Fez</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1028&amp;focus=maghrawa-emirate-of-fez" aria-label="Maghrawa emirate of Fez on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4553 944 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Maghrawa emirate of Fez lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4873 1200L4889 1294M4873 1200L4881 1071M4873 1200L4799 1289"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4889 1294h0M4881 1071h0M4799 1289h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4873 1200h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4873 1200h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>